  "outstanding": [
    "The nonzero test coefficient supplies two finite support conditions. The Gaussian example checks those lattice conditions and the actual metric inequalities, independently of the choice of test coefficient. The one-type count also uses its separate flag distribution and pointwise kernel bounds."
